{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_operations_deployment_kubernetes_k8s_manifest", "label": "Kubernetes-Manifest (StatefulSet, Services, RBAC)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/operations/deployment/kubernetes.mdx", "source_location": "Das vollstaendige Manifest", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Drei Dinge muessen sitzen: stabile Identitaet fuer stateful Actors, Seed-Discovery, und ein sauberer Shutdown-Pfad, damit Rolling Updates keinen Traffic verlieren. StatefulSet fuer vorhersagbare Identitaet und per-Pod-Volumes, Deployment wenn der State extern liegt. Nie replicas: 1 fuer stateful Actors - ein Ein-Replica-Cluster hat keinen Failover-Partner."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_operations_deployment_kubernetes_headless_service", "label": "Headless Service fuer Cluster-Gossip", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/operations/deployment/kubernetes.mdx", "source_location": "Headless Service fuer Cluster-Gossip", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "clusterIP: None liefert die Pod-IPs direkt per DNS, weil die Heartbeats des Failure Detectors auf spezifische Pod-IPs zielen und nicht auf eine load-balancete Abstraktion. App- und Management-Traffic gehen ueber den regulaeren Service."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_operations_deployment_kubernetes_kubernetesapiseedprovider", "label": "KubernetesApiSeedProvider", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/operations/deployment/kubernetes.mdx", "source_location": "ServiceAccount + RBAC", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Muss Pods listen koennen, die einem Label-Selector entsprechen; ohne das RBAC-Grant bekommt er 403 und der Cluster bildet sich nie. Auf dem ersten Pod ist die Seed-Liste nur er selbst - der Auto-Promote-to-Leader-Pfad."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_operations_deployment_kubernetes_prestop_sleep", "label": "preStop-Sleep", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/operations/deployment/kubernetes.mdx", "source_location": "preStop-Sleep", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Kritisch fuer saubere Rolling Updates: der Sleep gibt dem Load Balancer Zeit, keinen neuen Traffic mehr an den Pod zu schicken, bevor SIGTERM kommt. Ohne ihn laeuft SIGTERM gegen die LB-Deregistrierung und in-flight Requests sehen draining-Antworten."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_operations_deployment_kubernetes_termination_grace_period", "label": "terminationGracePeriodSeconds", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/operations/deployment/kubernetes.mdx", "source_location": "terminationGracePeriodSeconds", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Muss den preStop-Sleep PLUS die Shutdown-Pipeline abdecken; der Worst Case der Pipeline ist default-phase-timeout (5 s) mal der Anzahl der Phasen, die tatsaechlich Tasks haben - nicht mal zwoelf, denn eine leere Phase ist ein No-Op. Zu kurz heisst SIGKILL mittendrin: kein sauberes Leave, ungeflushte Journals, gekillte Requests."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_operations_deployment_kubernetes_probes", "label": "Readiness- und Liveness-Probes", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/operations/deployment/kubernetes.mdx", "source_location": "Readiness- + Liveness-Probes", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "/ready ist durch cluster-membership und cluster-transport abgesichert, App-Checks kommen via healthChecksOf(system).addReadiness dazu. /health beantwortet 'wuerde ein Neustart helfen' und haengt deshalb von nichts ausserhalb des Prozesses ab - eine Datenbank dort einzutragen wuerde bei einem gemeinsamen Ausfall die ganze Flotte neu starten, und die Neustarts wuerden nichts reparieren."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_operations_deployment_kubernetes_rununtilterminated", "label": "runUntilTerminated", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/operations/deployment/kubernetes.mdx", "source_location": "App-seitige Verdrahtung", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Installiert die SIGTERM/SIGINT-Handler und fuehrt die Shutdown-Pipeline aus. Es gibt keinen separaten Teardown-Schritt zu schreiben: beide bind()-Aufrufe haben ihr Unbind in service-unbind registriert und Cluster.join den Leave in cluster-leave, der Pod faellt also aus Service-Endpoints und Cluster, bevor die Actors stoppen."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_operations_deployment_kubernetes_rolling_update", "label": "Rolling Update mit automatischem Shard-Rebalancing", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/operations/deployment/kubernetes.mdx", "source_location": "Rolling Updates", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Pro Pod: terminating + preStop, 10 s LB-Drain, SIGTERM, Coordinated Shutdown (service-unbind, service-requests-done, service-stop, cluster-leave, actor-system-terminate), neuer Pod, Rejoin via Seed-Provider. Fuer sharded Entities passiert das Rebalancing automatisch."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_operations_deployment_kubernetes_k8s_manifest", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_operations_deployment_kubernetes_headless_service", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/operations/deployment/kubernetes.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_operations_deployment_kubernetes_k8s_manifest", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_operations_deployment_kubernetes_termination_grace_period", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/operations/deployment/kubernetes.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_operations_deployment_kubernetes_k8s_manifest", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_operations_deployment_kubernetes_prestop_sleep", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/operations/deployment/kubernetes.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_operations_deployment_kubernetes_k8s_manifest", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_operations_deployment_kubernetes_probes", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/operations/deployment/kubernetes.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_operations_deployment_kubernetes_k8s_manifest", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_operations_deployment_kubernetes_kubernetesapiseedprovider", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/operations/deployment/kubernetes.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_operations_deployment_kubernetes_probes", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_observability_overview_managementroutes", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/operations/deployment/kubernetes.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_operations_deployment_kubernetes_rolling_update", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_operations_deployment_kubernetes_prestop_sleep", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/operations/deployment/kubernetes.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, 